      "body": "# Independent exact-head delivery review — geometric NoRead fit\n\n**APPROVED for protected delivery of head `85c873ac2a9d36e79bf63bd02eea66c5c8139505` against base `1fc30e9c13387c7a88bfd8c787e93210f6d64773`. No material blocker was found.**\n\nReviewer: `/root/principal_mathematician`, nonauthor of the two fit source files and delivery documentation. This is a read-only exact-head/source/receipt/claim review, reusing the completed independent result audit rather than repeating model execution. No Cargo, model inference, fitting, source/Git change or new experimental campaign was performed. This exclusive note is the only new artifact. Protected CI/merge status is separate from this verdict.\n\nThe prior result audit remains unchanged at `result-adversarial-review.md`, SHA256 `325a9169f67a22166e13764d45bbf31d96a5889b9731045449b2014838ffee21`. It independently recounts all512 fit rows, CE and null values, all640 batches and RNG links per seed, eight checkpoint bindings per seed,37 frozen file identities and45 base-variable hashes. Its stated limits carry forward.\n\n## Source and execution bindings\n\nThe exact head is clean and contains only the six intended paths below. Both new driver source files match the executed and independently source-reviewed hashes: main `e6dadc47e61a97f447ff46c049343c37935c3f6fc770823b45f5514677767dad`, helper `f5178cf853e059f1ed4c66f1216d78b97da079784637b163c6443ba210755935`. Working bytes equal the committed blobs. The source base is unchanged.\n\nDelivery receipt SHA256 is `fa35be30af6ab70668332a64b6a6bc4ab91cd2e3c16a6bc38a0dafeb4de09011`. Every embedded execution and report exactly equals its retained original after the receipt's explicit precision-safe transformation of integers outside the JavaScript safe range into decimal strings. Report, manifest, history, input-identity and row hashes match actual saved files. The independent-result-review and preregistration hashes match their unchanged artifacts. No out-of-safe-range integer identity remains as a numeric JSON value in the derived receipt.\n\nThe exact initial→final RNG strings are seed1 `12355479550239716776`→`9347350181718662555` and seed2 `11629321088715907971`→`10697677911788535647`, agreeing with raw Rust u64 reports/checkpoints. These are recorded continuation identities; optimizer moments are explicitly absent, so exact AdamW continuation is not claimed.\n\nThe compressed executable identity matches the receipt, and decompression yields SHA256 `511122e619d8572eaa82201aa8b82438f4dc9aba228f66f3d76a87112135c9c7`, the executable bound by both actual fit wrappers. No claim is made that this review executed it.\n\n## Checks and result scope\n\nThe new fit example has two focused passing tests: answer-mask/exact-RNG handling and selected clipping/projection/independent copy. Each of the two check-mode attempts performs one backward with zero updates and evaluates32 original plus32 stress rows. These are128 check rows total, separate from the512 final fit rows. The prior NoRead deliverable's15 distinct focused passing cases plus these two driver cases constitute17 combined-scope cases; they are not17 new fit tests. The completed fits each perform640 backward/update batches at B8, not a tiny construction fit or a new dose sweep.\n\nThe full result record remains accurate: fitted source/native predictions agree512/512 and fitted native reproduces every legacy-parent prediction. Accuracy is458/512 for fitted/legacy and459/512 for zero/ablated. The only zero-to-fit changes are seed1 original: gain113, losses72/102. Seed1-original CE worsens slightly, seed1-stress improves and seed2 CE improves slightly without answer changes. The reported final nonzero q4 counts49/50 (all−1,0,+1) are distinct from cumulative flip counts371/50. No clipping, projection or saturation occurred.\n\nFor the final receipt I additionally checked the newly asserted median query-null probabilities and score ranges directly from saved integer fractions/scores. They match. The57952 actual head/position scalar comparisons and maximum11-Q24-unit discrepancy also match the raw source-null/native-null arrays. This scalar comparison is separated from downstream real-softmax/F32 versus LUT/Q24/Q16 logit differences. No scalar bit-exactness, whole-model integer qualification or energy claim is inferred.\n\nThe documentation preserves the copied-scalar intervention's actual scope: it removes retained-root/category/held-root/validity coefficients while retaining bias/token coefficients and all context/address/value behavior. It reverses the same three seed1-original predictions. Query-token/validity collinearity and the always-positive grammar preclude general geometric history-use or semantic-absence conclusions. Mixed effects and all negative rows remain reported.\n\n## Roadmap disposition\n\nThe current-state and project-track changes agree with the measured decision: retain fitted, zero and ablated scalar artifacts; end this fixed-dose scalar comparison; proceed to geometric attention output/composition from actual read.out/residual/decoder callers while inspecting remaining value/potential coefficient-width obligations. This does not authorize a final vocabulary-head substitution, a return to dense Q/K serving, another scalar sweep or a claim of geometric predictive superiority. Offline donor-weight/operator compilation and parallel D19/session work remain explicit and intact.\n\nNo additional test or model campaign is requested for delivery. The exact head is approved on the existing source review, executed scoped checks and loaded-result evidence.\n\n## Committed file identities\n\n| Path | Git blob | SHA256 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `crates/uor-r4-training/examples/attention-geometric-no-read-fit.rs` | `d059631fb748049639b873d1dd5334eac3b02744` | `e6dadc47e61a97f447ff46c049343c37935c3f6fc770823b45f5514677767dad` |\n| `crates/uor-r4-training/examples/attention-geometric-no-read-fit/fit.rs` | `1547ddd8b273d4549d5f26fe5bcedb58bba8ac24` | `f5178cf853e059f1ed4c66f1216d78b97da079784637b163c6443ba210755935` |\n| `docs/evidence/geometric-no-read-fit-2026-10-02.json` | `3c8a3c2391ba9a5eb3802e88bb9089d51235b429` | `fa35be30af6ab70668332a64b6a6bc4ab91cd2e3c16a6bc38a0dafeb4de09011` |\n| `docs/integration/current-state.md` | `3ad38af6f1f097ab1a8e5b090146a918c79d8d34` | `5d80fe723ff4234be2a9ef8cdfe175a3e03b9475be5f29948c853d879d7459c9` |\n| `docs/integration/geometric-no-read-fit-2026-10-02.md` | `3205bde8c7fb4f153bf13999f8d0b8c3c07e59d3` | `900dfb697c690a839f96990915259432778a557f31461b1a56c6cffdd07196a3` |\n| `docs/integration/project-track.md` | `5d933a1c6afd8b126b94d1e818c96dfda82a5862` | `bbf46c3493b408238bf2bdc8c58503ee302d68b9d7ca2ba2677c0e56f54fa9c7` |\n",
